From 5337c55703a16e7a745f8ea874ecccca3459baf3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "github-actions[bot]" <github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 20:56:33 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] mocha: NvMM-era display/decode compat for the legacy
 tegra stack

MEDIA:
- ACodec: skip metadata output negotiation for OMX.Nvidia.h264.decode
  (the blob does not support DynamicANWBuffer). The whole if/else must
  be skipped, otherwise err=OK falls into the else branch and trips
  CHECK(storingMetadataInDecodedBuffers()).
- MediaCodecList/OmxInfoBuilder/OMXStore/OMXNodeInstance: compatibility
  and enumeration adjustments for the old OMX components
- SoftwareRenderer/SurfaceUtils/CameraSource: adapt software YUV output
  and color conversion to an HWC1 environment without ANWBuffer metadata
- Codec2InfoBuilder: enable debug logging for c2 component enumeration
- services/mediacodec/Android.bp: adjust codec2 service build flags

This kernel has no msdec/vdec drivers, so NVIDIA hardware decoding is
unavailable and software decoding is the only path.
